  "candidate": "framing-views-worker",
  "worker_operation": "hvcc-annexb-",
  "reference": "ffmpeg-framing-views-native",
  "contract": [
    "Parse hvcC with HvcConfigParser. In all mode write every unit with HvcAnnexBWriter. In decoder mode HvcDecoderConfigWriter accepts records whose declared array types are VPS, SPS, PPS, prefix SEI or suffix SEI. A disallowed array refuses the record as a whole.",
    "The pinned hevc_mp4toannexb initializer converts those same five array types and refuses other declared types. In decoder mode the public FFmpeg log gives the first disallowed declaration after a reference refusal. The candidate array index is printed in trace.",
    "Compare Annex B output in record order. Each unit begins with a four-byte start code. Fold kind 1 with the type and length and bytes including the header, and kind 7 with the count and decoder refusal absence. Fold kind 8 for a parse or filter refusal, adding the type for the typed decoder refusal.",
    "Loading is outside the operation. Parser and filter setup, writing, folding and teardown are inside."
  ],
  "required_profiles": [
    "script",
    "reference-written",
    "authored"
  ],
  "required_targets": [
    "aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu",
    "thumbv7neon-unknown-linux-gnueabihf"
  ],
  "iterations": 50,
  "minimum_pairs": 30,
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "pending_module_requirements": [
    "A missing or Annex B configuration is outside the hvcC parser and FFmpeg initializes it as unconverted input",
    "The strict hvcC parser refuses a three-byte sample length field and FFmpeg initializes the record",
    "The all-array writer preserves every declared array while FFmpeg rejects unsupported array types, including empty declarations",
    "The hvcC parser enforces the caller record, array or NAL count limit and FFmpeg initializes the record",
    "The hvcC parser refuses a partial array header without a type and FFmpeg logs a disallowed type zero for it"
  ],
